# GitHub OAuth2 Implementation Walkthrough

## Overview

Successfully implemented GitHub OAuth2 authentication for the Crypto Price Aggregator application. Users can now log in using their GitHub accounts instead of basic HTTP authentication.

## Implementation Summary

### Backend Changes

#### 1. Dependencies ([pom.xml](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/pom.xml))

Added Spring Security OAuth2 client dependency:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-oauth2-client</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

#### 2. Domain Layer

**New File**: [User.java](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/domain/User.java)

Created JPA entity to persist OAuth2 authenticated users:
- Maps to `oauth2_users` table
- Stores GitHub profile information (ID, username, email, name, avatar)
- Tracks creation and last login timestamps
- Uses Lombok for cleaner code

**New File**: [V3__create_oauth2_users.sql](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/resources/db/migration/V3__create_oauth2_users.sql)

Flyway migration script creating:
- `oauth2_users` table with appropriate columns
- Indexes on `github_id`, `username`, and `last_login`
- Unique constraints on GitHub ID and username

#### 3. Repository Layer

**New File**: [UserRepository.java](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/repository/UserRepository.java)

JPA repository interface with query methods:
- [findByGithubId(String githubId)](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/repository/UserRepository.java#16-23) - Find user by GitHub ID
- [findByUsername(String username)](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/repository/UserRepository.java#24-31) - Find user by username
- [existsByGithubId(String githubId)](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/repository/UserRepository.java#32-39) - Check user existence

#### 4. Service Layer

**New File**: [CustomOAuth2UserService.java](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/service/CustomOAuth2UserService.java)

Custom OAuth2 user service:
- Extends `DefaultOAuth2UserService`
- Loads user information from GitHub
- Creates new users or updates existing ones
- Maps GitHub attributes to User entity
- Adds custom attributes (user ID, roles) to OAuth2User

#### 5. Controller Layer

**New File**: [AuthController.java](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/controller/AuthController.java)

REST controller for authentication operations:
- `GET /api/auth/user` - Returns current user info
- `GET /api/auth/status` - Returns authentication status
- `POST /api/auth/logout` - Handles logout

#### 6. Security Configuration

**Modified**: [SecurityConfig.java](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/config/SecurityConfig.java)

Major updates:
- Added `@RequiredArgsConstructor` and injected [CustomOAuth2UserService](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/service/CustomOAuth2UserService.java#24-86)
- Configured `.oauth2Login()` with:
  - Custom login page ([/frontend/index.html](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/frontend/index.html))
  - Success redirect URL
  - Custom OAuth2 user service
- Added `.logout()` configuration
- Permitted `/login/**`, `/oauth2/**`, and `/api/auth/status` endpoints
- Updated CORS to include ngrok web interface
- Removed OAuth2 comment block (now implemented)

#### 7. Application Configuration

**Modified**: [application.properties](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/src/main/resources/application.properties)

Added OAuth2 client registration:
```properties
spring.security.oauth2.client.registration.github.client-id=${GITHUB_CLIENT_ID}
spring.security.oauth2.client.registration.github.client-secret=${GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET}
spring.security.oauth2.client.registration.github.scope=read:user,user:email
spring.security.oauth2.client.registration.github.redirect-uri={baseUrl}/login/oauth2/code/{registrationId}
```

#### 8. Docker Configuration

**Modified**: [docker-compose.yml](file:///home/pran/anotherDrive/javaCodes/CPA/docker-compose.yml)

Added environment variables to app service:
```yaml
- GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=${GITHUB_CLIENT_ID}
- GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=${GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET}
```

